From 123ac97d208451392d8e48fed2e3c1489b88e92e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:30:48 +1200
Subject: [PATCH v18 8/8] arm64: dts: rockchip: enable the NPU on
 rk3576-rock-4d

Enable both NPU cores and their IOMMUs in the ROCK 4D device tree.

Make vdd_npu_s0 the supply of the NPU power domain. The power domain
driver is what switches the NPU rail on and off, with the domain, once
it handles the RK3576 NPU domain supply ("pmdomain: rockchip: manage the
RK3576 NPU domain supply", sent separately). Without that, nothing holds
vdd_npu_s0, which is not always-on on this board, and the regulator core
turns it off as unused.

The cores also get npu-supply, which the binding requires and the
RK3588 boards set as well. No driver uses it at the moment.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts      | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
index f068794e48d4..72b251d396fe 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
@@ -722,6 +722,10 @@ &pcie0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pd_npu {
+	domain-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+};
+
 &pinctrl {
 	hdmi {
 		hdmi_tx_on_h: hdmi-tx-on-h {
@@ -779,6 +783,24 @@ wifi_en_h: wifi-en-h {
 	};
 };
 
+&rknn_core_0 {
+	npu-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_mmu_0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_core_1 {
+	npu-supply = <&vdd_npu_s0>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknn_mmu_1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &sai6 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
